          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Phoriospongia",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "The live sponge (Fig. 19 A) is irregularly massive, bright red and covered by algal turf. The fragment preserved in alcohol changed the color to grey, with an uneven surface. It is very hard and friable and rich in sediments. SKELETON. The ectosome and the choanosome are almost completely constituted by columns of grains, with scattered spicules among the foreign bodies. SPICULES. Styles (Fig. 19 B – C) with stepped tips, 260 – (294.5, 24.2) – 340 μm × 2.5 – (2.8, 0.8) – 5 μm; C- and S-shaped sigmas (Fig 19 D), 28 – (37.2) – 42 μm; arcuate isochelae (Fig. 19 E), 9 – (12.5) – 14 μm.",
