          "description": "Thin smooth crust, size 4 x 3.5 cm, thickness less than 0.5 mm (Fig. 7 C). Color dark brown with purple veins; interiorly the sponge is orange – brown. Pigment grains in the lighter parts of the surface form areolae-like formations of approx. 100 µm in diameter. Consistency soft. Skeleton. Feebly developed bundles of megascleres traverse the choanosome vertically ending at and pushing up the surface to cause microconules. No tangential surface skeleton. Spicules. Strongyles only, no further spicules. Strongyles (Figs 7 A – B), straight, isodiametric, with evenly rounded (not swollen) apices, often with wide axial cavity, 213 - 252.7 - 277 x 3 - 3.9 - 4.5 µm. Ecology. Under coral rubble at 5 m",
